<p class="updated">Last updated: 2 October 2026</p>

<p class="lead">
  Handball Coachboard sets no cookies, has no accounts and doesn't collect personal data.
</p>

<h2>Who runs this site</h2>
<p>
  Handball Coachboard is run by {owner}. For questions about your privacy, email <a
    href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a
  >.
</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>
  This site sets no cookies, first-party or third-party, and loads no advertising. The
  statistics below work without cookies too. That's why there is no cookie banner.
</p>

<h2>The board</h2>
<p>
  The board keeps your drawing in your browser's local storage, on your own device, so it's
  still there next time. It never leaves your device unless you share it.
</p>
<p>
  A shared link carries the drawing after the <code>#</code> in the address. Browsers don't send
  that part to any server, so we never see what you draw. QR codes are made in your browser too.
</p>

<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>
  The site is hosted by Cloudflare. To deliver pages and protect the site against abuse,
  Cloudflare processes technical data such as your IP address and browser type, as any web
  server does. We don't use that data to identify you. See the <a
    href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
    rel="noopener">Cloudflare privacy policy</a
  >.
</p>

<h2>Statistics</h2>
<p>
  To learn whether trainers use the board and how fast it is on their phones, the board pages
  load <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare Web
    Analytics</a
  >. The other pages load no script at all.
</p>
<p>
  It counts page views and measures loading speed, without cookies, without anything stored
  in your browser and without fingerprinting. It sends the address of the page without the
  part after the <code>#</code> or <code>?</code>, so never your drawing; the page you came
  from; your browser, operating system and device type; your country; and how fast the page
  loaded and responded. Cloudflare drops your IP address at its nearest data center and
  doesn't store it, and keeps the statistics for six months.
</p>
<p>
  A shared link opens <code>/board/link/</code> and a QR code <code>/board/qr/</code>. That
  tells us how often shared boards are opened, and nothing about what is on them.
</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>When something changes, we update this page and the date at the top.</p>
